## Document layout (Orchestration-Oriented Development)

This project uses the OOD document-driven workflow. The documents under
`docs/` are the state — there is no JSON state machine.

| dir | what it holds | read it when |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/plans/` | the contract for each epic: intent, **acceptance criteria**, task breakdown, **file-ownership map**. `plan:NNN` is the key. | before doing any work; it is the source of truth |
| `docs/adr/` | decisions and why (terse, AI-read) | when a choice's rationale matters |
| `docs/specs/` | the living spec — what the system does, synced to reality | to understand current behaviour |
| `docs/reports/` | completion markers & journal, incl. `NNN-inspection.html` with `<h2>Verdict: GO|NOGO</h2>` | to see what's done / inspection outcomes |

Conventions:
- **Docs are HTML and visual by default.** Lead with diagrams — Mermaid
  (`<pre class="mermaid">…</pre>`) for sequence / flowchart / architecture / state,
  or inline SVG for precise static figures. Prefer a diagram over a wall of text.
- The plan in `docs/plans/` is authoritative. Any Agent Teams task list is a
  disposable projection of it.
- A task that must pass inspection is marked `[gate:inspect]` and references
  `plan:NNN`. It cannot complete until `docs/reports/NNN-inspection.html` says
  `Verdict: GO` (enforced by a TaskCompleted hook).
- Stay within your assigned file-ownership boundary; do not edit another
  teammate's files (there is no worktree isolation in team mode).
